      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Not sure there's any way around this on VRChat's end -- the way I check for the presence of the player's menu is to scan for protected objects in the UIMenu layer, and presumably there are no UIMenu objects active when you're holding shift to point at people.\nNative support in Udon for this kind of menu behaviour via events (to check if the quick menu is open/the player is pointing at things) would solve this (and might have other uses as well).",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
